346:<Evidence kind="observed" /> **The reviewer copy.** The drift-check source records a deployed reviewer missing its mandatory establish-the-diff step while the upstream copy contained it. The incident was filed August 5; the check was committed August 6. Its five-day interval describes the stale deployment. Comparing deployed bytes with the source makes that discrepancy visible, but doesn't recover a per-session loading history or count incorrect reviews.[^drift]
347-
348:<Evidence kind="observed" /> **Sibling instructions.** One harness-specific instruction file carried superseded doctrine for six weeks after its canonical sibling changed. The parity gate committed August 5 checks a declared relationship between those files. It doesn't require every document to be identical. The separate live-document staleness check catches a named obsolete assertion outside that pair; it leaves dated historical records alone.[^parity][^staleness]
349-
350:<Evidence kind="observed" /> **Workflow copies that needed different repairs.** The synchronization source records both missing upstream review checks and local copies with stricter conditional-verdict handling. The August 11 implementation preserves per-project rosters and refuses local-ahead overwrites. That refusal protects the difference from erasure; it doesn't certify the difference as correct or promote it into shared policy.[^workflow]
